Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 03:28:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 109/119] docs: the shadow fillers, the sky's real unit, and a
 fifth round of tests

ConsoleReference gains r_SceneReferredSkyPeakLuminance and rewrites
r_SceneReferredNishitaScale around what the dome actually is: not a third
brightness system with no documented unit, but a physically formed
single-scattering integral whose output is an engine radiance like everything
else - which makes the shipped "Sun intensity multiplier 50" a claim of 500 000
lux against a physical 133 000, and makes 0.37 a derivation rather than a guess.
Both entries carry what the number does NOT fix: the model's zenith and its
illuminance are 1.9 stops apart and one scalar cannot satisfy both, and the sky
peak bounds an approximation because the dome has no sun sprite at all.

README and SceneReferredContent stop describing SVOGI, the fogs, the clouds and
the snow as deliberate breakage and describe them as fixed, with the three
consequences a lighter actually needs: SVOGI's voxel cache stays in unexposed
units on purpose so its cvars keep their stock meaning, hue-shifted bounce light
means the codec ceiling is being hit again, and lit particles were 1.65 stops hot
until now so old smoke and dust will read darker.

The calibration doc's section 2 is rewritten end to end. It used to say the scale
could not be derived from source; it can, and the section is now the derivation,
the measurement that confirms it, the predicted 32 000 lux to check against, the
probe staleness that the _rec stamp does not catch, and the trap that a probe's
Diffuse multiplier scales its blend weight rather than its brightness.

Also written down, because it is the kind of thing that gets applied twice: the
correction is carried once. r_SceneReferredNishitaScale 0.37 and a preset
multiplier of 18.5 are the same fix by two routes, and doing both is 1.4 stops
dark. ReC_Physical.env deliberately keeps the shipped 50.

Fifth round of the user's test checklist (in scene-notes, not in git): SVOGI with
the aperture and WITHOUT e_svoTI_Apply 0 as an escape hatch, fog that does not
glow at night, clouds that meet the sky without a step, snow at half res that
does not flatten the frame behind it, particles that sit in the scene, and one
number to read - the dome's illuminance at a 45-degree sun with the sun out of
frame.

